  "description": "EVOQAK crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C86 H136 Co7 Ho3 N4 O38. From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Ho1A (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3A (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co4A (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.933-4.644 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.53-147.56°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C86H136Co7Ho3N4O38. Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
